{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-gaussian-solves-q-heat","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-gaussian-solves-q-heat","kind":"proposition","title":"Reeb-invariant $q$-Gaussian solves the $q$-heat equation (archimedean)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-exponential-taylor"],"tags":["q-heat-equation","q-gaussian","heat-kernel","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.qGaussianSolvesQHeat","text":"q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-gaussian-solves-q-heat\"></a><p>Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}^n</code> with the archimedean realisation of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian, the Reeb-invariant <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Gaussian</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  G_q(t, x) = \\bigl(4\\pi q^{-2} t\\bigr)^{-n/2} \\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{q^2  |x|^2}{4t}\\right)</code></pre>\n<p>is a fundamental solution of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\partial_t G_q = -\\Delta_q G_q, \\qquad \\lim_{t \\downarrow 0} G_q(t, \\cdot) = \\delta_0.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-gaussian-solves-q-heat.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"21.8.2"}
